{
  "id": "SP03Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Hysterectomy",
  "description": "A hysterectomy removes your uterus to treat fibroids, cancer, endometriosis, or other gynecologic conditions. Your surgeon can use open surgery, vaginal approach, or laparoscopic minimally invasive technique depending on your situation. The open or vaginal approach typically requires a 1-2 day hospital stay and 4-6 weeks of recovery; laparoscopic surgery is faster, with a typical recovery of 2-3 weeks. You'll have some vaginal bleeding and cramping for a few weeks. Most people experience relief from their original symptoms. After recovery, you can return to normal activities including exercise and intercourse. This type of procedure can be performed various ways, including an open surgical approach or a minimally invasive laparoscopic technique, and the cost may vary depending on the method used.",
